<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean '96 PPI up 3.5 pct vs 3.4 pct rise in '95.</title>
<headline>S.Korean '96 PPI up 3.5 pct vs 3.4 pct rise in '95.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's producer price index (PPI) rose 3.5 percent in 1996 against growth of 3.4 percent in 1995, the Finance and Economy Ministry said on Sunday.</p>
<p>					 Dec 96     Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p>    PPI (pct, yr-on-yr)	    +3.5	 +3.8	 +3.4</p>
<p>    PPI (pct, month-to-month)    +0.4	 -0.1	 +0.7</p>
<p>    PPI (base=1990)		 121.5	121.0	117.4</p>
<p>The ministry said sharp rises in international crude oil prices were the biggest factor behind this year's growth of the PPI, a leading indicator of future price trends.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
